     "transcript": [
      {
       "start": 3.4,
       "end": 8.0,
       "text": "Every edge into E is a lower bound.",
       "sceneId": "a01-longest"
      },
      {
       "start": 8.0,
       "end": 12.4,
       "text": "Put the bounds on a line: 3, 5, 7.",
       "sceneId": "a01-longest"
      },
      {
       "start": 12.4,
       "end": 17.2,
       "text": "To meet all three, x[E] must be 7 or more.",
       "sceneId": "a01-longest"
      },
      {
       "start": 17.2,
       "end": 21.8,
       "text": "The smallest feasible value is the longest path.",
       "sceneId": "a01-longest"
      },
      {
       "start": 22.2,
       "end": 27.0,
       "text": "Three blocks: A below C; A and C left of B.",
       "sceneId": "a02-max"
      },
      {
       "start": 27.0,
       "end": 32.6,
       "text": "The minimum, 2, meets only C's bound; B lands on A.",
       "sceneId": "a02-max"
      },
      {
       "start": 32.6,
       "end": 36.6,
       "text": "The maximum, 3, meets both.",
       "sceneId": "a02-max"
      },
      {
       "start": 37.0,
       "end": 40.6,
       "text": "Could a constraint graph have a cycle?",
       "sceneId": "a03-acyclic"
      },
      {
       "start": 40.6,
       "end": 44.8,
       "text": "Label every block with its place in pos.",
       "sceneId": "a03-acyclic"
      },
      {
       "start": 44.8,
       "end": 49.4,
       "text": "Both 'left of' and 'below' need first in pos.",
       "sceneId": "a03-acyclic"
      },
      {
       "start": 49.4,
       "end": 54.0,
       "text": "Along any edge the place grows: no cycle.",
       "sceneId": "a03-acyclic"
      },
      {
       "start": 54.4,
       "end": 59.2,
       "text": "Compute all 14,400 pairs.",
       "sceneId": "a04-fit"
      },
      {
       "start": 59.2,
       "end": 62.2,
       "text": "Not one overlaps.",
       "sceneId": "a04-fit"
      },
      {
       "start": 62.2,
       "end": 66.0,
       "text": "But 720 do not fit 10 × 8.",
       "sceneId": "a04-fit"
      },
      {
       "start": 66.0,
       "end": 71.267,
       "text": "Outline unused and density never change; they cannot compare pairs.",
       "sceneId": "a04-fit"
      },
      {
       "start": 71.667,
       "end": 76.689,
       "text": "Swap E and D in pos: the E–D relation changes.",
       "sceneId": "a05-twins"
      },
      {
       "start": 76.689,
       "end": 81.489,
       "text": "Yet the coordinates are identical: both relations hold.",
       "sceneId": "a05-twins"
      },
      {
       "start": 81.489,
       "end": 86.289,
       "text": "Conversely, the same box can hide a different packing.",
       "sceneId": "a05-twins"
      },
      {
       "start": 86.289,
       "end": 91.978,
       "text": "14,400 pairs, only 9,056 packings.",
       "sceneId": "a05-twins"
      },
      {
       "start": 92.378,
       "end": 96.578,
       "text": "Some textbooks define 'below' as 'above'.",
       "sceneId": "a06-mirror"
      },
      {
       "start": 96.578,
       "end": 102.489,
       "text": "It is a vertical mirror: swap pos and neg.",
       "sceneId": "a06-mirror"
      },
      {
       "start": 102.489,
       "end": 106.089,
       "text": "Check the convention before you read on.",
       "sceneId": "a06-mirror"
      },
      {
       "start": 106.489,
       "end": 112.622,
       "text": "Cost: n(n−1)/2 pairs, two DP passes, O(n²).",
       "sceneId": "a07-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 112.622,
       "end": 116.422,
       "text": "Building the graphs and the DP do the work.",
       "sceneId": "a07-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 116.422,
       "end": 121.022,
       "text": "Search uses swaps; the number of pairs explodes.",
       "sceneId": "a07-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 121.422,
       "end": 125.689,
       "text": "The longest path gives the most compact coordinates.",
